e for  the good jobs of the future thinking  about investments in your own training  and education over the course of your  career is just a really smart idea um  one of the things people should be doing  is asking their employers for what  opportunities there are for advancement  asking your Union what can you do to  help help support these kind of  your letters looking into things like  joint Union and management programs that  support these kind of career letters for  example there's there's programs that  will help people go from a nursing  assistant to an LPN to a registered  nurse and if you can think of supporting  those kinds of trajectories you can  really carve out a career that really  let's let you punch punch the ticket to  the middle class I think that's that's  good advice young people have lots of  opportunities and they have to create  new ones along with the partnership of  the Department of Labor and good  employers and good labor organizations  so thank you very much it's been my  pleasure  [Music]
 

